  "conclusion": "The first non-fixed-index absolute torsion jet is efficiently public but obeys an exact normalization law and collapses to the already-public combined EDS/parity factor on Kummer-invariant, secp256k1-like cases. The exact n+1 and n-1 sections collapse to the same public factor. Higher torsion jets, near-period sections through radius four, and all retained products of weight at most four show no exact decoder and no case above the matched 95% random-label envelope.",
  "claim_boundary": [
    "Bounded toy structural evidence, not an asymptotic lower bound.",
    "The first-jet identity is derived from the division-polynomial composition law and its standard local leading term; a source-pinned formal proof is still pending.",
    "The screen does not cover unbounded jets, nonlocal theta sections, p-adic analytic continuation, or arbitrary circuits.",
    "No external point, key, wallet, or production-sized target is accepted."
  ]
